              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+type"}> geometric homotopy type
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+homotopy+type"} cohesive homotopy type
          %h2#References References
          %p
            The concept of typing in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
            is implicit in
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gottlob+Frege"} Gottlob Frege
          %ul
            %li#Russell03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Russell"}> Bertrand Russell
              , appendix of
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Principles_of_Mathematics"} The principles of mathematics
              1903 (
              %a{:href => "http://fair-use.org/bertrand-russell/the-principles-of-mathematics/appendix-b"}> online
              )
          %p where it has the famous passage
          %blockquote
            %p
              Every propositional function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x)
              — so it is contended - has, in addition to its range of truth, a range of significance, i.e. a range in which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              must lie if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x)
              is to be a proposition at all, whether true or false. This is the first point in the theory of types; the second point is that ranges of significance form types, i.e. if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              belongs to the range of significance of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(x)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              may be varied;
          %p Also
          %ul
            %li#Russell08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Russell"}> Bertrand Russell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mathematical Logic as Based on the Theory of Types
            %li#RussellWhitehead10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Russell"}> Bertrand Russell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alfred+Whitehead"} Alfred Whitehead
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Principia+Mathematica"} Principia Mathematica
          %p
            and later work by Russell, where it is used to prevent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paradoxes"} paradoxes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/liar%27s+paradox"} liar's paradox
            (via a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ramified+type"}> ramified hierarchy
            ” of types) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell%27s+paradox"} Russell's paradox
            (via an “extensional hierarchy” of types). This then evolved into the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+type+theory"}> simple type theory
            ”:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Leon Chwistek, The Theory of Constructive Types: Principles of Logic and Mathematics, Krakow: University Press, 1925, 98 pp. Extracted from the Annales de la Société Polonaise de Mathématique. (In DjVu format)
                %a{:href => "http://www.monoskop.org/Leon_Chwistek"} Linked from this page, under Bibliography, On logic and mathematics.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alonzo+Church"}> Alonzo Church
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Formulation of the Simple Theory of Types
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/2266170?seq=1#page_scan_tab_contents"} JSTOR
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alonzo+Church"}> Alonzo Church
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Schröder’s Anticipation of the Simple Theory of Types
                %strong 10
                (1976) 407-411 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00176047"}> doi:10.1007/BF00176047
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p This is reviewed for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              Jean van Heijenoort,
              = succeed "," do
                %em From Frege to Gödel
          %p
            On the modern notion of types in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            and in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+types"} data types
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+languages"} programming languages
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Martin-Löf82"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Constructive Mathematics and Computer Programming
              %strong 104
              (1982) 153-175 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0049-237X(09)70189-2"}> doi:10.1016/S0049-237X(09)70189-2
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The introduction of (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-rule"} J-rule
            for)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            in “intuitionistic”/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            is originally due to:
          %ul
            %li#MartinLoef75
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
                , §1.7 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An intuitionistic theory of types: predicative part
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Logic Colloquium ‘73, Proceedings of the Logic Colloquium
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 80
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0049-237X(08)71945-1"} doi:10.1016/S0049-237X(08)71945-1
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.131.926"} CiteSeer
            %li
              %p
                Bengt Nordström, Kent Petersson, Jan M. Smith, §8.1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Programming in Martin-Löf’s Type Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cse.chalmers.se/research/group/logic/book/"} webpage
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cse.chalmers.se/research/group/logic/book/book.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/NordstromPeterssonSmith-TypeTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The development of that to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            followed insights by (
            %a{:href => "#HofmannStreicher98"}> Hofmann-Streicher 98
            ) and others and was laid out in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
          %p Survey of the history of type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://plato.stanford.edu/entries/type-theory/"} Type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harley+Eades"}> Harley Eades
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Type Theory and Applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://metatheorem.org/includes/pubs/comp.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/EadesTypeTheoryAndApplications.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Of course there is also discussion of formalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            originating in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computer+science"} computer science
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+types"} data types
          %p Surveys of and introductions:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"} Per Martin-Löf
                (notes by
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Sambin"} Giovanni Sambin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Intuitionistic type theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://archive-pml.github.io/martin-lof/pdfs/Bibliopolis-Book-retypeset-1984.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MartinLofIntuitionisticTypeTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"}> Thomas Streicher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Investigations into intensional type theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/HabilStreicher.pdf"} pdf
            %li#MartinLoef96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Meanings of the Logical Constants and the Justifications of the Logical Laws
                %strong 1
                1 (1996) 11-60 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://docenti.lett.unisi.it/files/4/1/1/6/martinlof4.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MartinLofOnTheMeaning96.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Geuvers"}> Herman Geuvers
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to type theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.ru.nl/~herman/PUBS/IntroTT-improved.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolaas+G.+de+Bruijn"}> Nicolaas G. de Bruijn
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the roles of types in mathematics
                %strong 8
                (1992) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://alexandria.tue.nl/repository/freearticles/597627.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/deBriujn-TypesInMath.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"}> Bart Jacobs
                ,
                %em Categorical Type Theory
                PhD. Thesis, University of Nijmegen (1991) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.ru.nl/B.Jacobs/PAPERS/PhD.ps"} ps
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JacobsCategoricalTypeTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"}> Bart Jacobs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Categorical Logic and Type Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 141
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/studies-in-logic-and-the-foundations-of-mathematics/vol/141"} ISBN:978-0-444-50170-7
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://people.mpi-sws.org/~dreyer/courses/catlogic/jacobs.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.ru.nl/B.Jacobs/CLT/bookinfo.html"} webpage
            %li#Constable11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Constable"}> Robert Constable
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Triumph of Types: Creating a Logic of Computational Reality
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.cs.uoregon.edu/research/summerschool/summer11/"} Types, Semantics and Verification
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.uoregon.edu/research/summerschool/summer11/lectures/Triumph-of-Types-Extended.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/ConstableTriumphOfTypes.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Bauer17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spartan Type Theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.andrej.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/12/Spartan-Type-Theory.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_theory"} type theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intuitionistic_type_theory"} intuitionistic type theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typed_lambda_calculus"} typed lambda calculus
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curry%E2%80%93Howard_correspondence"} Curry-Howard correspondence
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Per_Martin-L&#246;f"} Per Martin-Löf
          %p
            Textbook accounts on type theory in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+languages"} programming languages
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhaohui+Luo"}> Zhaohui Luo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Computation and Reasoning – A Type Theory for Computer Science
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/computation-and-reasoning-9780198538356"} ISBN:9780198538356
                %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Zhaohui-Luo-4/publication/243770570_Computation_and_Reasoning_A_Type_Theory_for_Computer_Science/links/54d0dc6b0cf29ca81103f26a/Computation-and-Reasoning-A-Type-Theory-for-Computer-Science.pdf"} pdf
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (via the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+constructions"} calculus of constructions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carl+A.+Gunter"}> Carl A. Gunter
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Semantics of Types in Programming Languages
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Logic+in+Computer+Science"} Handbook of Logic in Computer Science
                Vol 3:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantic structures
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/handbook-of-logic-in-computer-science-9780198537625"} ISBN:9780198537625
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://seclab.illinois.edu/wp-content/uploads/2011/04/Gunter94.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Harper"}> Robert Harper
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Practical+Foundations+for+Programming+Languages"} Practical Foundations for Programming Languages
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cambridge.org/us/academic/subjects/computer-science/programming-languages-and-applied-logic/practical-foundations-programming-languages-2nd-edition?format=HB"} ISBN:9781107150300
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~rwh/pfpl/2nded.pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p &amp;lbrack;p. xvii:&amp;rbrack; Types are the central organizing principle of the theory of programming languages. Language features are manifestations of type structure. The syntax of a language is governed by the constructs that define its types, and its semantics is determined by the interactions among those constructs. The soundness of a language design—the absence of ill-defined programs—follows naturally. The purpose of this book is to explain this remark.
          %p
            Further discussion of type theory in the context of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+programming"}> functional
            )
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+languages"} programming languages
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Thompson"}> Simon Thompson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Type+Theory+and+Functional+Programming"} Type Theory and Functional Programming
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.kent.ac.uk/people/staff/sjt/TTFP"} webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.kent.ac.uk/people/staff/sjt/TTFP/ttfp.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Girard89
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"} Jean-Yves Girard
                (translated and with appendiced by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Taylor"} Paul Taylor
                and
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Lafont"} Yves Lafont
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Proofs and Types
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => ""} ISBN:978-0-521-37181-0
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.paultaylor.eu/stable/Proofs+Types.html"} webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.paultaylor.eu/stable/prot.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benjamin+Pierce"}> Benjamin Pierce
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Types and Programming Languages
                %a{:href => "http://www.cis.upenn.edu/~bcpierce/tapl/index.html"} book page
          %p
            Discussion aimed at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            include
          %ul
            %li#Taylor99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Taylor"}> Paul Taylor
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Practical+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Practical Foundations of Mathematics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.paultaylor.eu/~pt/prafm/html/index.html"} webpage
            %li#Taylor
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Taylor"}> Paul Taylor
                ,
                %em Foundations for computable topology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.paultaylor.eu/ASD/foufct/abstract.html"}> web
                )
          %p
            Work leading up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            includes
          %ul
            %li#HofmannStreicher98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hofmann"}> Martin Hofmann
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"} Thomas Streicher
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The groupoid interpretation of type theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Sambin"} Giovanni Sambin
                et al. (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twenty-five years of constructive type theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/twenty-five-years-of-constructive-type-theory-9780198501275"} ISBN:9780198501275
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/venedig.ps.gz"} ps
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HofmannStreicherGroupoidInterpretation.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"}> Thomas Streicher
                ,
                %em Identity Types and Weak Omega-Groupoids
                2006
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/TALKS/uppsala.pdf.gz"} pdf.gz
          %p
            Formalization of parts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            in type theory is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"}> Thierry Coquand
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://wiki.portal.chalmers.se/cse/pmwiki.php/ForMath/ForMath"} ForMath
          %p
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
          %ul
            %li#CoquandSpiwack
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"}> Thierry Coquand
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Spiwack"} Arnaud Spiwack
              %em Towards constructive homological algebra in type theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://assert-false.net/arnaud/papers/Towards%20constructive%20homological%20algebra%20in%20type%20theory.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Thoughts about type theory and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaphysics"} metaphysics
            are in
          %ul
            %li#MartinLoef90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A path from logic to metaphysics
              = succeed "," do
                %em Nuovi problemi della logica e della filosofia della scienza
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://archive-pml.github.io/martin-lof/pdfs/A-path-from-logic-to-metaphysics-1991.pdf"} pdf
          %p For a type theory suitable for non-cartesian monoidal categories see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A practical type theory for symmetric monoidal categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.00818"} arXiv:1911.00818
          %p Further online resources include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Type theory summer school Göteborg 2005, (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cse.chalmers.se/research/group/logic/TypesSS05/program.html"}> materials
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/tagged/type-theory"} type-theory questions
                on MathOverflow
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://cstheory.stackexchange.com/questions/tagged/type-theory"} type-theory questions
                on CS StackExchange
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://lists.seas.upenn.edu/mailman/listinfo/types-list"} types mailing list
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://lists.seas.upenn.edu/mailman/listinfo/types-announce"} types-announce mailing list
